<h2 id="last-weeks-most-unjustifiably-overlooked-release">Last Week&apos;s Most Unjustifiably Overlooked Release</h2><h3 id="uncle-acid-and-the-deadbeats-%E2%80%93-shapes-of-midnight-occult-rockmetal">Uncle Acid and the Deadbeats &#x2013; <em>Shapes of Midnight</em> (occult rock/metal)</h3><p>I didn&apos;t give this one a proper listen before posting last week&apos;s roundup, we got the promo early, but, after a quick sample I wrote it off as a good album from a band I respected but traditionally Wasn&apos;t For Me&#x2122;. I should have paid more heed to <a href="https://www.heavyblogisheavy.com/2026/09/18/uncle-acid-and-the-deadbeats-shapes-of-midnight/" rel="noreferrer">Jordan&apos;s review</a> though, because&#x2014;while I&apos;m not qualified to comment on whether this is the best Uncle Acid and the Deadbeats album&#x2014;I can say its doing a whole lot more for me than any of their previous records have, or similar releases of its ilk have been lately.</p><p>In comparison to the shark-jumping self-parody of the new <a href="https://www.heavyblogisheavy.com/2026/09/10/green-lung-necropolitan/" rel="noreferrer">Green Lung</a> record, <em>Shapes of Midnight</em> oozes class and sincerity, along with a compelling mastery of its craft. It also rocks super hard. Along with the expected malaize of psychedelic <strong>Black Sabbath </strong>worship that pervades their sound, &quot;Psycho on the Loose&quot; sounds like <strong>Turbonegro </strong>covering <em>Turbo-</em>era Judas Priest, while &quot;Don&apos;t Let it Control You&quot; almost sounds like <strong>Motorhead</strong> mixed with <strong>Hellhammer</strong>, with lots of bass fills that bring to mind &quot;Born to Be Wild&quot;. Indeed, bassist Justin Smith may well be the man of the match, delivering a <em>Meddle</em>-esque <strong>Pink Floyd</strong> trudge on &quot;When Evil Wakes&quot; and plenty of Geezer Butler-isms throughout that help make <em>Shapes of Midnight </em>a surprisingly vital pre-summer soundtrack as the weather starts to get warmer down under.</p>
<!--kg-card-begin: html-->
<iframe style="border: 0; width: 100%; height: 120px;" src="https://bandcamp.com/EmbeddedPlayer/album=3483953274/size=large/bgcol=333333/linkcol=e99708/tracklist=false/artwork=small/transparent=true/" seamless><a href="https://uncleacidandthedeadbeats.bandcamp.com/album/shapes-of-midnight-album?ref=heavyblogisheavy.com">Shapes Of Midnight [Album] by Uncle Acid and the deadbeats</a></iframe>
<!--kg-card-end: html-->
