ontent/images/2026/09/a2222956488_10.jpg";s:6:"medium";s:5:"image";}}s:8:"xml_base";s:0:"";s:17:"xml_base_explicit";b:0;s:8:"xml_lang";s:0:"";}}}s:40:"http://purl.org/rss/1.0/modules/content/";a:1:{s:7:"encoded";a:1:{i:0;a:5:{s:4:"data";s:29174:"<h2 id="top-pick">Top Pick?</h2><h3 id="game-over-%E2%80%93-face-the-end-2025">Game Over &#x2013; <em>Face the End</em> (2025)</h3><img src="https://storage.ghost.io/c/8b/c6/8bc603be-b831-44f6-8ffb-773be5bd45c8/content/images/2026/09/a2222956488_10.jpg" alt="Release Roundup: 9/18/26"><p>No, that&apos;s not a mistake. Nothing&apos;s really doing it this week. Once upon <a href="https://www.heavyblogisheavy.com/2017/12/21/year-review-best-non-2017-albums/" rel="noreferrer">a time</a>, a <strong>Carly Rae Jepsen </strong>double-abum would be cause for celebration, but not in September of 2026. Similarly, while I seemed to enjoy 2016&apos;s <em>For All Kings </em>a lot more than most, and while the new <strong>Anthrax </strong>album isn&apos;t as bad as its <a href="https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=uqbhWhN4F74&amp;pp=0gcJCf4LAYcqIYzv&amp;ref=heavyblogisheavy.com">AI Babadook magician</a>-laden promo cycle suggested it might be, it&apos;s still far from recommendable. </p><p>The need for some better thrash had me looking in the direction of Italian thrashers <strong>Game Over</strong>, but their new one&#x2014;while perfectly fine&#x2014; isn&apos;t really all that either. However, I remember referring to last year&apos;s <em>Face the End </em>in our Discord as &quot;the best Anthrax album in years&quot;, but never ended up actually writing about it anywhere, so I&apos;m choosing to give it a belated highlight here, in lieu of any better options.</p><p>Going back to it now, my assessment of the album still stands. New vocalist Danny Schiavina gives hints of both John Bush and Joey Belladonna and the riffs are about as righteous as you can hope for from a longrunning re-thrash band these days. The quality of Game Over&apos;s records has always hovered  &quot;decent but not exciting&quot;, but I&apos;d say <em>Face the End </em>sits only behind <em>Crimes Against Reality </em>(2016) in their discography and is well worth a listen if you overlooked it last year, or&#x2014;like me&#x2014;are just looking for a good thrash fix.</p>
<!--kg-card-begin: html-->
<iframe style="border: 0; width: 100%; height: 120px;" src="https://bandcamp.com/EmbeddedPlayer/album=136079512/size=large/bgcol=333333/linkcol=e99708/tracklist=false/artwork=small/transparent=true/" seamless><a href="https://gameoverofficial.bandcamp.com/album/face-the-end?ref=heavyblogisheavy.com">Face The End by Game Over</a></iframe>
<!--kg-card-end: html-->
<p><strong>See also: </strong>that <a href="https://harlottmetal.bandcamp.com/album/exsequiis?ref=heavyblogisheavy.com" rel="noreferrer"><strong>Harlott album</strong></a> from last week.</p><h2 id="release-roundup">Release Roundup</h2><p><a>Aletheya &#x2013; </a><a href="Aletheya%20&#x2013;%20Chance%20To%20Reborn">Chance To Reborn</a> (prog metal)</p><p>Anoreksi &#x2013; <a href="https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=uZe6hhpeHJQ&amp;ref=heavyblogisheavy.com">Insignificance</a> (melodeath)</p><p><a>Asenblut &#x2013; </a><a href="https://youtu.be/qwiyU0fs_fw?ref=heavyblogisheavy.com">Urgewalt</a> (ass, butt)</p><h3 id="anthrax-%E2%80%93-cursum-perficio-thrash">Anthrax &#x2013; <em>Cursum Perficio</em> (thrash) </h3><figure class="kg-card kg-embed-card"><iframe width="200" height="113" src="https://www.youtube.com/embed/Pj5u8OagODo?feature=oembed" frameborder="0" allow="accelerometer; autoplay; clipboard-write; encrypted-media; gyroscope; picture-in-picture; web-share" referrerpolicy="strict-origin-when-cross-origin" allowfullscreen title="Anthrax - It&apos;s For the Kids"></iframe></figure><h3 id="beck-%E2%80%93-ride-lonesome-folk">Beck &#x2013; <em>Ride Lonesome</em> (folk) </h3><figure class="kg-card kg-embed-card"><iframe width="200" height="113" src="https://www.youtube.com/embed/VqQmgHcIHN0?feature=oembed" frameborder="0" allow="accelerometer; autoplay; clipboard-write; encrypted-media; gyroscope; picture-in-picture; web-share" referrerpolicy="strict-origin-when-cross-origin" allowfullscreen title="Beck - Ride Lonesome (Official Music Video)"></iframe></figure><p><a>Bees Made Honey In The Vein Tree &#x2013; </a><a href="https://beesmadehoneyintheveintree.bandcamp.com/album/in-between-strides?ref=heavyblogisheavy.com">In Between Strides</a> (shoegaze)</p><p>Blackment &#x2013; <a href="https://blackment.bandcamp.com/album/pandemonium-portrait?from=search&amp;search_item_id=1025489594&amp;search_item_type=a&amp;search_match_part=%3F&amp;search_page_id=5756548278&amp;search_page_no=1&amp;search_rank=1&amp;search_sig=c1a234b8efda867e1a05a081a853b769&amp;ref=heavyblogisheavy.com">Pandemonium Portrait</a> (melowdic metal)</p><h3 id="the-bleeding-%E2%80%93-godless-communion-death-metal">The Bleeding &#x2013; <em>Godless Communion</em> (death metal) </h3>
