";s:7:"attribs";a:0:{}s:8:"xml_base";s:0:"";s:17:"xml_base_explicit";b:0;s:8:"xml_lang";s:0:"";}}}}}i:8;a:6:{s:4:"data";s:0:"";s:7:"attribs";a:0:{}s:8:"xml_base";s:0:"";s:17:"xml_base_explicit";b:0;s:8:"xml_lang";s:0:"";s:5:"child";a:4:{s:0:"";a:6:{s:5:"title";a:1:{i:0;a:5:{s:4:"data";s:34:"Video Premiere: Beware the Cyclops";s:7:"attribs";a:0:{}s:8:"xml_base";s:0:"";s:17:"xml_base_explicit";b:0;s:8:"xml_lang";s:0:"";}}s:11:"description";a:1:{i:0;a:5:{s:4:"data";s:122:"Deathcore wrecking crew Complexant reveal a bludgeoning condemnation of the modern surveillance state in their new video. ";s:7:"attribs";a:0:{}s:8:"xml_base";s:0:"";s:17:"xml_base_explicit";b:0;s:8:"xml_lang";s:0:"";}}s:4:"link";a:1:{i:0;a:5:{s:4:"data";s:46:"https://www.heavyblogisheavy.com/2026/09/17/v/";s:7:"attribs";a:0:{}s:8:"xml_base";s:0:"";s:17:"xml_base_explicit";b:0;s:8:"xml_lang";s:0:"";}}s:4:"guid";a:1:{i:0;a:5:{s:4:"data";s:24:"6aabe3549c65ae000122128e";s:7:"attribs";a:1:{s:0:"";a:1:{s:11:"isPermaLink";s:5:"false";}}s:8:"xml_base";s:0:"";s:17:"xml_base_explicit";b:0;s:8:"xml_lang";s:0:"";}}s:8:"category";a:1:{i:0;a:5:{s:4:"data";s:9:"Premieres";s:7:"attribs";a:0:{}s:8:"xml_base";s:0:"";s:17:"xml_base_explicit";b:0;s:8:"xml_lang";s:0:"";}}s:7:"pubDate";a:1:{i:0;a:5:{s:4:"data";s:29:"Thu, 17 Sep 2026 12:59:24 GMT";s:7:"attribs";a:0:{}s:8:"xml_base";s:0:"";s:17:"xml_base_explicit";b:0;s:8:"xml_lang";s:0:"";}}}s:32:"http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/";a:1:{s:7:"creator";a:1:{i:0;a:5:{s:4:"data";s:14:"Bridget Hughes";s:7:"attribs";a:0:{}s:8:"xml_base";s:0:"";s:17:"xml_base_explicit";b:0;s:8:"xml_lang";s:0:"";}}}s:29:"http://search.yahoo.com/mrss/";a:1:{s:7:"content";a:1:{i:0;a:5:{s:4:"data";s:0:"";s:7:"attribs";a:1:{s:0:"";a:2:{s:3:"url";s:111:"https://storage.ghost.io/c/8b/c6/8bc603be-b831-44f6-8ffb-773be5bd45c8/content/images/2026/09/a2088121259_10.jpg";s:6:"medium";s:5:"image";}}s:8:"xml_base";s:0:"";s:17:"xml_base_explicit";b:0;s:8:"xml_lang";s:0:"";}}}s:40:"http://purl.org/rss/1.0/modules/content/";a:1:{s:7:"encoded";a:1:{i:0;a:5:{s:4:"data";s:2569:"<img src="https://storage.ghost.io/c/8b/c6/8bc603be-b831-44f6-8ffb-773be5bd45c8/content/images/2026/09/a2088121259_10.jpg" alt="Video Premiere: Beware the Cyclops"><p>Like many die-hard music fans, I have an increasingly complicated relationship with streaming services. Spotify has managed to become the poster child for enshittification, AI slop, and militarized tech bros, while Tidal often froze and didn&#x2019;t have enough depth in their metal library. Qobuz was delightful in many ways, but was also missing a number of heavy artists. Apple Music, by default, became my backup music service after Bandcamp and physicals. Shockingly, the app surfaces a band that wasn&#x2019;t on my radar, but immediately becomes part of my heavy rotation. Case in point: Aussie tech deathcore wrecking crew <strong>Complexant</strong>.&#xa0;</p><p>Their debut album, <em>Apex</em>, is a testament to the wild deathcore scene in Australia. Crisp production sets the stage for bludgeoning riffs to expand in a moody atmosphere, letting clean vocals exchange blows with harsh growls that echo over intensely aggressive songwriting. Complexant captures the perfect balance between ignorant (complimentary) death metal and technical, semi-polished deathcore. The sound is juuuust clean enough to give each element the space to breathe while not sacrificing the suffocating, pummeling heaviness.&#xa0;</p><p>Perhaps ironically, given that tech dystopia is part of the reason I discovered Complexant at all, their new visualizer for &#x201c;Cyclops&#x201d; is a cutting condemnation of the surveillance state enabled by tech corporations. Rendered in stark black, white, and red, the video flickers between song lyrics and the horrors of modern society: cameras watching your every move, environmental destruction, an unjust &#x201c;justice&#x201d; system, and war.&#xa0;</p><p>Watch the video below and follow Complexant on <a href="https://complexant.bandcamp.com/?ref=heavyblogisheavy.com"><u>Bandcamp</u></a>.&#xa0;</p><figure class="kg-card kg-embed-card"><iframe width="200" height="113" src="https://www.youtube.com/embed/cw2kMREXhfk?feature=oembed" frameborder="0" allow="accelerometer; autoplay; clipboard-write; encrypted-media; gyroscope; picture-in-picture; web-share" referrerpolicy="strict-origin-when-cross-origin" allowfullscreen title="Complexant - Cyclops (Official Visualiser)"></iframe></figure><p>Music: Complexant</p><p>Lyrics: Dan Greigsy&#xa0;</p><p>Mixed and Mastered: Christian Donaldson&#xa0;</p><p>Graphic Design: Taigan Harris, Bleeding Art Collective</p>";s:7:"attribs";a:0:{}s:8:"xml_base";s:0:"";s:17:"xml_base_explicit";b:0;s:8:"xml_lang";s:0:"";}}}}}i:9;a:6:{s:4:"data";s:0:"";s:7:"attribs";a:0:{}s:8:"xml_base";s:0:"";s:17:"xml_base_explicit";b:0;s:8:"xml_lang";s:0:"";s:5:"child";a:4:{s:0:"";a:6:{s:5:"title";a:1:{i:0;a:5:{s:4:"data";s:50:"Album Premiere: Have you met your Suffering Quota?";s:7:"attribs";a:0:{}s:8:"xml_base";s:0:"";s:17:"xml_base_explicit";b:0;s:8:"xml_lang";s:0:"";}}s:11:"description";a:1:{i:0;a:5:{s:4:"data";s:123:"Is any of this worth it? With Suffering Quota's riffs...maybe. Listen to the full album now before it drops on Sept. 18th. ";s:7:"attribs";a:0:{}s:8:"xml_base";s:0:"";s:17:"xml_base_explicit";b:0;s:8:"xml_lang";s:0:"";}}s:4:"link";a:1:{i:0;a:5:{s:4:"data";s:93:"https://www.heavyblogisheavy.com/2026/09/16/album-premiere-have-you-met-your-suffering-quota/";s:7:"attribs";a:0:{}s:8:"xml_base";s:0:"";s:17:"xml_base_explicit";b:0;s:8:"xml_lang";s:0:"";}}s:4:"guid";a:1:{i:0;a:5:{s:4:"data";s:24:"6aaa9cc250103e00017ffe59";s:7:"attribs";a:1:{s:0:"";a:1:{s:11:"isPermaLink";s:5:"false";}}s:8:"xml_base";s:0:"";s:17:"xml_base_explicit";b:0;s:8:"xml_lang";s:0:"";}}s:8:"category";a:1:{i:0;a:5:{s:4:"data";s:9:"Premieres";s:7:"attribs";a:0:{}s:8:"xml_base";s:0:"";s:17:"xml_base_explicit";b:0;s:8:"xml_lang";s:0:"";}}s:7:"pubDate";a:1:{i:0;a:5:{s:4:"data";s:29:"Wed, 16 Sep 2026 13:50:00 GMT";s:7:"attribs";a:0:{}s:8:"xml_base";s:0:"";s:17:"xml_base_explicit";b:0;s:8:"xml_lang";s:0:"";}}}s:32:"http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/";a:1:{s:7:"creator";a:1:{i:0;a:5:{s:4:"data";s:14:"Bridget Hughes";s:7:"attribs";a:0:{}s:8:"xml_base";s:0:"";s:17:"xml_base_explicit";b:0;s:8:"xml_lang";s:0:"";}}}s:29:"http://search.yahoo.com/mrss/";a:1:{s:7:"content";a:1:{i:0;a:5:{s:4:"data";s:0:"";s:7:"attribs";a:1:{s:0:"";a:2:{s:3:"url";s:111:"https://storage.ghost.io/c/8b/c6/8bc603be-b831-44f6-8ffb-773be5bd45c8/content/images/2026/09/sufferingquota.jpg";s:6:"medium";s:5:"image";}}s:8:"xml_base";s:0:"";s:17:"xml_base_explicit";b:0;s:8:"xml_lang";s:0:"";}}}s:40:"http://purl.org/rss/1.0/modules/content/";a:1:{s:7:"encoded";a:1:{i:0;a:5:{s:4:"data";s:2049:"<img src="https://storage.ghost.io/c/8b/c6/8bc603be-b831-44f6-8ffb-773be5bd45c8/content/images/2026/09/sufferingquota.jpg" alt="Album Premiere: Have you met your Suffering Quota?"><p>Life is short, then you die. The interim is filled with the humiliations and horrors of capitalism, the cruelty of your fellow humans, and a seemingly unstoppable march towards the apocalypse. Are we having fun yet?</p><p>If your answer was &#x201c;yes,&#x201d; then today&#x2019;s album is for you. Dutch grindcore quartet <strong>Suffering Quota </strong>are set to release their fourth full-length album, <em>Sisyphean Life</em>, via 7 Degrees Records and Tartarus Records this Friday, September 18th.&#xa0;</p><p>Blistering, caustic, and utterly merciless, the album takes the harsh whirlwind of grindcore and infuses it with the muscular devastation of death metal. The former hooks you, but the latter stops you dead in your tracks. Lean, mean buzzsaw guitars twist into ugly riffs that channel old school death metal, shapeshifting into structures that pack heavyweight brutality into 90-second tracks. <em>Sisyphean Life</em> is unmistakably grindcore, but speaks to death metal fans with equal heft.&#xa0;Here to grind, lingering &apos;til death. </p><p><em>Sisyphean Life </em>will be released on Friday, September 18th. Stream the full album below and pre-order on <a href="https://sufferingquota.bandcamp.com/album/sisyphean-life?ref=heavyblogisheavy.com"><u>Bandcamp</u></a>.&#xa0;</p>
<!--kg-card-begin: html-->
